WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.380
-What are we gonna do, Buzz?
-Use your head!

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.900
But I don't wanna use my head!

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.660
(ALL SCREAMING)

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.620
-(THUD)
-REX: Ow!

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.740
MAN 1: Speed.
MAN 2: Marker.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.460
MAN 3: Okay, and pull back.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:16.860
(WHEELS SQUEAKING)

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.100
(BURPING) Whew!

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.300
-I don't remember eating that.
-MAN: Cut.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.300
-(GROANING) I can't believe this.
-That's the fifth time.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.220
-What row is that guy in?
-Sorry.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.900
I had that bean burrito for lunch.
Okay, I'm all right now. Sorry.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.420
MAN: And action.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.980
I'm packing you an extra pair of shoes
and your angry eyes just in case.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:41.420
And if you get hungry,
here's some cheese puffs. And a key.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.700
I don't know what it's for,
but you never know.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.660
MAN 1: Speed.
MAN 2: Marker.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.180
MAN 3: And action.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.660
Whoo!

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:49.820
(CRASHING)

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.940
(LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY)

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.860
Could...? Should we just...?

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.500
Should that just be part
of the movie now?

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.420
He lost... He lost his string.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.180
And the golf ball,
if you have time for golf.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.220
And a plastic steak
and a rubber ducky and a yo-yo.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.340
-Who's behind?
-Mine.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.060
MAN: All right, cut. Good take.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.700
What good acting.
That was a good take.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.460
You're such a cute little bottom.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.620
Look at you. Look at you.
Look at you. Look at you.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.300
In fact, I think I feel a song comin' on.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.020
-(THUDDING)
-(FEEDBACK)

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.140
Mr. Mike, I'm so sorry.
Did I hurt your equipment?

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.300
You gotta aim it right here at my flipper.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.980
I'm not a very good catch.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.620
-Okay, I'm ready for another take.
-MAN: Let's go again.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.740
(THUDDING)

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.900
(WHEEZING)

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.860
Oh, no! Oh, no,
I think I swallowed my squeaker!

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.060
(COUGHING)

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.500
And an extra-bouncy bouncy ball.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.580
And some extra teeth.
Be careful, they chatter.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.100
-(TEETH CHATTERING)
-Whoa!

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.460
MAN 1: Marker.
MAN 2: And action.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.380
(TAPPING)

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.860
(SNICKERING)

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.580
We'll be back before Andy gets home.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.780
What? What're you laughing about?

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.580
Huh? (LAUGHING)

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.180
Real funny, Woody.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.660
MAN: We're losing our light.
Wipe it off and let's go again.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.260
Golly bob howdy.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.540
What? What's so funny? Woody!

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.860
(SPRINGING)

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.980
(LAUGHING)

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.060
Huh?

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:33.700
-Darn it, Woody!
-MAN: Okay, let's go again.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.340
And crayons, in case you get bored.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.380
And some blue Play-Doh.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.940
(GROANING)

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.500
Isn't this exciting, Heimlich?
Our first day of shooting.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.940
Oh, yeah, yeah, it's so exciting!

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.260
You know, I can't believe you talked
them into making A Bug's Life 2.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:55.100
Oh, oh, yeah,
I can hardly believe it also.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.100
Oh, but there's a little baby tiny thing
I forgot to tell you.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.180
What's that, Heimlich?

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:05.300
Well, it's a "2" movie,
but it's not A Bug's Life 2.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.980
What...? I don't understand.
What is it then?

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.460
MAN: And action.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.340
-(CRASHING)
-(BUGS SCREAMING)

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.460
MAN 1: Speed.
MAN 2: Wait. Let me check focus.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.380
So, did you make it
into the first Toy Story?

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.060
In the letterbox copy,

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:19.820
you can see my arm
grabbing Woody's ankle.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:20.940
What are you gonna do next?

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.340
Well, I'm up for this villain
in a toothpaste commercial.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.740
-Wow, that's great.
-Really?

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:28.740
And a dime, call me.
And monkey chow.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.420
Monkey chow? For what?

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.940
Well, for the monkeys, of course.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.500
-Come on, monkeys.
-(SCREECHING)

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.980
That's it. I draw the line at monkeys.
Get my agent on the phone!

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.180
MAN 1: Marker.
MAN 2: And action.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.820
It's your choice, Woody.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.260
You can go back, or you can stay
with us and last forever.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.980
(FARTING)

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:53.420
Good heavens. Was that me?
(LAUGHING)

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.780
Oh, my. (FARTING) I am so sorry.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:01.060
I guess that's why they call me
Stinky Pete. Whoo!

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.580
MAN: Okay, let's cut.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.780
We are so glad you came.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.620
Bye-bye. Bye-bye. Bye-bye.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.940
Bye-bye, now. Bye. Bye-bye.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.980
Remember, please discard all candy
wrappers and popcorn containers

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.220
in the nearest trash receptacle.
Thank you.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:20.700
Okay, bye-bye, now. Bye-bye. Bye.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:21.980
(LAUGHING)

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.820
Okay.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.380
Are they all gone?

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.460
Is everybody gone?

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.140
Huh?

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.980
(SQUEAKING) Good. Oh, my gosh,
my cheeks are killing me.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:38.060
I can't keep smiling like this anymore.
I am exhausted.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.220
I think I need a break.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.380
A little break? Okay.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:43.660
Whew.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:48.220
(WOODY'S ROUNDUP
THEME PLAYING)

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.620
CHORUS: ♪ Woody's Roundup

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.460
♪ Come on, and gather round

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.060
♪ Woody's Roundup

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.900
♪ Where nobody wears a frown

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.460
♪ Bad guys go runnin'

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.540
♪ Whenever he's in town

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.980
♪ He's the rooting-est
Tooting-est, shooting-est

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.860
♪ Hooting-est cowboy around

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.940
♪ Woody's Roundup ♪

